### `kernel/src/rmsnorm.cuh` (ticket 06, kernel-abi-02)
RMSNorm / LayerNorm for the pointwise path. Adapted from the reference
RMSNorm math (`ops/kernel/rmsnorm.cuh`: the per-vector sum-of-squares ->
rsqrtf(mean + eps) -> scaled-epilogue pipeline; the PDL-synced bf16x2
row-geometry variants and the engine's Tensor dispatch are not ported —
C++ state the flat C ABI of ADR 0001 forbids, and the PDL calls are
stripped in favor of plain `<<<>>>` launches) and its LayerNorm sibling
(`ops/kernel/layer_norm.cuh`: the center-then-normalize form). The
normalization math is ported 1:1 for the ABI's 1-D vector contract: the
sum of squares, the rsqrtf reciprocal, and the out = value * inv * weight
epilogue. The ABI's `center` argument centers first (base[i] = x[i] -
center[i], the "LayerNorm mode"); the reference's data-dependent Welford
mean/m2 dispatch is not ported (the ABI centers with an explicit vector,
per the header contract). A single 1024-thread block grid-strides over n
(the reference's bf16x2 / warp-tiled row variants are the performance-gate
material, ADR 0007); fp32 internal math, bf16 in/out. Self-contained;
compiles standalone in the leaf.

### `kernel/src/embed_gather.cuh` (ticket 06, kernel-abi-02)
Dense embedding gather. 1:1 port of the reference's dense embedding gather
(`ops/kernel/embed_gather.cuh`: `embed_gather_dense_kernel` — the grid-
stride row copy `out[i] = table[ids[i/d] * d + i % d]`). The quantized
table variants (Q6 / W8 / FP8 code + scale planes, the grouped per-token
launchers) and the shape-specific route dispatch are not part of the v1
ABI contract — the ABI table is a dense bf16 [vocab][hidden] matrix, so
only the dense gather's math (the row selection and the grid-stride copy)
is ported; the quantized paths are later-ticket material. Self-contained;
compiles standalone in the leaf.

### `kernel/src/argmax.cuh` (ticket 06, kernel-abi-02)
Greedy (argmax) sampling. Adapted from the reference argmax kernel
(`ops/kernel/argmax.cuh`: `argmax_kernel` — the per-row block reduce with
the value/lower-index winner rule, plus the shared-memory
`argmax_block_reduce` aggregation; the winner rule
`value > best || (value == best && index < best_index)` is ported 1:1).
The reference reads bf16 logits with a physical/valid row pair for padded
rows, and the launcher dispatches a tiled atomic-cas route for wide
vocabularies; the ABI contract is an f32 [batch][vocab] matrix with no
padding (vocab == the valid row count), so the single-tile finite route is
ported 1:1 with the input typed to f32, and the tiled-atomic route is
deferred to the performance gate (ADR 0007). Self-contained; compiles
standalone in the leaf.

