### `kernel/src/bf16_gemm.cuh` (ticket 29, kernel-abi-10, GitHub #29)
bf16 GEMM (the logits path for the W8-dequantized lm_head). No reference
equivalent in the reference fork's ABI surface: the reference engine
consumes the dequantized lm_head through its own tensor-core GEMM dispatch
(C++ state the flat C ABI of ADR 0001 does not carry). This kernel follows
the proven rowsplit FMA pattern of the ticket-22 NVFP4 prefill GEMM
(nvfp4_gemm_prefill.cuh — the rowsplit "rows-of-W x tokens" tiling, fp32
FMA accumulation, shared-memory k-chunk staging, bf16 store) with the NVFP4
dequant staging replaced by a plain bf16 weight read (the A1 artifact
dequant produces a bf16 lm_head). The tensor-core MMA (the later
performance-gate material, ADR 0005/0007) is deliberately not used: v1 is
the correctness-first scalar-FMA baseline. Self-contained; compiles
standalone in the leaf.

